{"base_rate":0.39755766621438265,"brier":0.16959538670284938,"bss":0.2918937628755035,"bss_hi":0.39394710745203054,"bss_lo":0.1859305562310219,"chart":{"base":[577.5,153.9],"fp":[257.9,224.0],"lead":"62,271.6 272,244.8 482,198.7 692,121.4","note":{"base":"skill 0.29 — higher than 44% of cities","fp":"low end +6pp, high end +21pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.9 °C — better than 86% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 9%; promised 95% → rained 75%"},"rel":"79.1,426.5 338.2,333.8 660.2,142.4"},"country":"NL","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.13234735413839893,"ess":289.8341205507659,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Breda</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Breda rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>81%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>7%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 737 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nGINNEKEN, 4.4 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.29, ranked 75 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(42&ndash;108) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>7%</b></td><td class='num'>208</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'><b>14%</b></td><td class='num'>87</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>28%</td><td class='num'><b>26%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>58%</td><td class='num'><b>35%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>83%</td><td class='num'><b>56%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>81%</b></td><td class='num'>222</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Breda</b> <span class=\"muted\">NL</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.29</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>42&ndash;108\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>737 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Breda &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Breda\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.86798076923077,378.5 88.51724137931035,327.60919540229884 155.42695652173913,244.84057971014494 264.3184615384615,130.0 351.09260273972603,52.90410958904113 408.2686486486487,18.0 408.2686486486487,27.83783783783781 351.09260273972603,112.7397260273973 264.3184615384615,209.33333333333334 155.42695652173913,318.69565217391306 88.51724137931035,369.44827586206895 58.86798076923077,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"237.2890094979647\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"237.2890094979647\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.86798076923077,355.75 88.51724137931035,331.7931034482759 155.42695652173913,287.04347826086956 264.3184615384615,256.0 351.09260273972603,177.56164383561642 408.2686486486487,86.86486486486484\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 7% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 208 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.86798076923077\" cy=\"355.75\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 9%&amp;#10;It rained 14% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 87 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"88.51724137931035\" cy=\"331.7931034482759\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 28%&amp;#10;It rained 26% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"155.42695652173913\" cy=\"287.04347826086956\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 58%&amp;#10;It rained 35% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"264.3184615384615\" cy=\"256.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 83%&amp;#10;It rained 56% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"351.09260273972603\" cy=\"177.56164383561642\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 81% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 222 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"408.2686486486487\" cy=\"86.86486486486484\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(40%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Breda the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.35) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.17).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>37%</td><td class='num'>0.173</td><td class='num'>14.3%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>53%</td><td class='num'>0.240</td><td class='num'>13.1%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>198</td><td class='num'>25%</td><td class='num'>0.267</td><td class='num'>14.4%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'>0.348</td><td class='num'>11.7%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":51.58656,"lon":4.77596,"n":737,"n_cities":134,"name":"Breda","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.002451923076923077,"n":208,"obs":0.07211538461538461,"sig":true},{"hi":0.16400000000000034,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.08620689655172414,"n":87,"obs":0.13793103448275862,"sig":false},{"hi":0.41,"lo":0.16400000000000034,"mean":0.2752173913043478,"n":69